# Static-site quality

## HTML

- Use semantic HTML landmarks and a logical heading hierarchy.
- Every meaningful image needs accurate alternative text; decorative images need `alt=""`.
- Use buttons for actions and links for navigation.
- Keep page-specific content in the appropriate template or existing JSON data source.

## CSS and responsive layout

- Prefer mobile-first CSS and test layouts at narrow and wide viewport sizes.
- Reuse existing design tokens, classes, and component patterns where possible.
- Avoid inline styles and `!important` unless there is a documented compatibility reason.
- Images must be responsive: constrain width, preserve aspect ratio, and avoid layout overflow.

## JavaScript and data

- Keep JavaScript dependency-free and compatible with modern browsers.
- Do not use `eval` or inject untrusted content with `innerHTML`.
- Only use same-origin data paths unless the user explicitly approves an external integration.
- Validate JSON syntax and preserve the existing data shape unless all consumers are updated together.

## Before completing a change

- Check for broken asset paths, dead links, console errors, and visual overflow.
- Verify the affected page(s) locally using `./serve.sh`.
- State which files changed and any manual checks still required.
